      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Scientist (Nutrition and Metabolism) Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 02 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Scientist (Nutrition and Metabolism) What you will be working on We are seeking a proactive and detail-oriented candidate to support a research project focused on nutrition interventions involving various local cuisines. The role involves supporting study coordination, managing research logistics, conducting data collection activities, planning and preparing intervention meals, and assisting in the preparation of scientific reports and documentation. The job responsibilities include the following: Coordinate and support the day-to-day operations of a research project on dietary intervention Plan and assist in the preparation and delivery of meals based on the study protocol. Manage logistics including participant recruitment, scheduling of visits and meal delivery. Perform study monitoring, study progress and ensure all research activities comply with ethical and safety guidelines. Manage adverse event documentation. Liaise with both internal teams and external vendors to ensure smooth study execution. Conduct nutrient analysis of the meals and participants nutrient intake data. Analysis and interpretation of data and preparation of the study report. What we are looking for Qualification in nutrition, food science, biomedical science, sports science, or related field. At least 3 years of experience in research coordination of human studies. Familiarity with research logistics, participant coordination, and data collection tools. Comfortable with field-based work and hands-on measurements, able to work flexible hours. Organised, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and within a team. Able plan and prepare multi-ethnic meals for nutrition intervention. Knowledge in nutrient analysis is an added advantage. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Manager/Senior Manager, Product Owner (Job Matching) (DX1) Skills and Workforce Development Agency Closing in 3  day(s) Analyst (Defence Capabilities) MINDEF Closing on 11 Oct 2026 Manager/Senior Manager, Research, Data Analytics and Insights (ICPD) [ Skills and Workforce Development Agency Closing in 5  day(s) Senior Manager (Research Engagement), SIR/RA MSF Closing on 04 Oct 2026 Statistician (Household Surveys & Expenditure) MTI- Dept of S Closing on 28 Sep 2026 Manager/Senior Manager (Research & Analytics), SIR/RA MSF Closing on 17 Oct 2026 Assistant Director/Senior Assistant Director (Research and Analytics) MSF Closing on 04 Oct 2026 Manager/Senior Manager (Research and Analytics) MSF Closing on 04 Oct 2026 Scientist (Nutrition and Metabolism) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 02 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
