      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Temporary Senior Executive Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 03 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Successful candidates will be offered a 11.5-month contract with the Academic Affairs Department. What you will be working on Plan, process and manage admissions, enrolment and examination activities for part-time courses Handle queries and offer advice to course applicants, students, and academic staff Collaborate with both academic and non-academic staff to ensure efficient course management and smooth administration of examinations Manage and maintain accurate and up-to-date student records Conduct data verification and liaise with vendors to resolve any system-related issues Plan, implement and monitor projects and initiatives for part-time courses Contribute to TP and department ad-hoc projects and initiatives as needed Compile data for reporting purposes Provide general administrative support for the division, ensuring proper documentation is maintained. What we are looking for At least 3 years of relevant work experience is preferred Detail-oriented with analytical and problem-solving skills, and a good team player Independent and self-motivated, with the ability to follow through on projects and deliver quality work Good written and verbal communication skills, coupled with strong interpersonal and administrative skills Able to effectively manage multiple tasks and projects to meet deadlines IT-savvy, proficient in Microsoft Office applications and possess knowledge of AI technologies and their practical applications About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Senior Executive / Careers & Internship Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Sep 2026 Senior Manager / Manager, Procurement, CMD MOM Closing on 30 Sep 2026 Assistant Manager / Manager, Transformation and Systems, FMMD MOM Closing on 30 Sep 2026 Assistant Manager / Manager, Grant Governance, Corporate Management De MOM Closing on 30 Sep 2026 Senior Executive, Service Quality (1-year temp) Health Sciences Authority Closing in 4  day(s) Manager/Senior Manager, Partnerships and Innovation (ICPD) [1 - year T Skills and Workforce Development Agency Closing in 5  day(s) Manager/Assistant Director (Planning), Community Relations Unit MND Closing on 30 Sep 2026 SENIOR EXECUTIVE, ACAD ADMIN & OPERATIONS - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 27 Sep 2026 Temporary Senior Executive Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 03 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
