      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (AI, Innovation) Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 30 Sep 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is We are looking for a motivated and enthusiastic individual with experience in applying artificial intelligence (AI) in the business context, The role focuses on leveraging AI tools and solutions to drive business innovation, strengthen data-driven decision-making and enable intelligent automation. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing future-ready business professionals who can apply AI strategically, critically, and responsibly to create sustainable organisational and societal value. What you will be working on Teaching & Student Development Conduct lectures, tutorials, student consultations, and supervise industry-based projects and internships. Teach and facilitate applied learning in areas such as AI for business innovation, AI-enabled decision-making, agentic AI, intelligent automation, and advanced analytics. Guide students in identifying business opportunities, analysing and redesigning workflows, prototyping AI-enabled solutions, and developing evidence-based business cases. Develop students’ ability to critically evaluate AI-generated outputs and make sound decisions based on data, evidence, business considerations, and human judgement.Support students’ learning and development through mentoring, coaching, and appropriate academic interventions. Support students’ learning and development through mentoring, coaching, and appropriate academic interventions. Organise student activities, industry visits, overseas learning journeys, and experiential learning opportunities to promote holistic development. Curriculum, Assessment & Learning Design Lead or contribute to the development and delivery of subjects in areas such as AI for Business Innovation and AI-enabled Decision Making, including assessments, assignments, marking, and moderation activities. Evaluate and enhance curriculum quality, lesson design, delivery methods such as e-learning, flipped classroom, and blended learning, as well as assessment practices through effective teaching and learning strategies. Contribute to subject reviews, curriculum development, accreditation exercises, and programme enhancement initiatives. Digital, Applied & Industry-Relevant Learning Embed applied AI practices into curriculum design, including generative AI, machine learning applications, agentic AI, intelligent automation, data analytics, business intelligence, workflow redesign, and rapid prototyping. Facilitate students’ experimentation with appropriate AI platforms and tools to develop and validate products, services, processes, and business-model innovations. Translate current industry practices into meaningful and effective learning experiences that strengthen students’ workplace readiness and applied problem-solving capabilities. Industry Collaboration & Professional Practice Participate actively in professional development activities, industry projects, consultancy work, and applied research initiatives. Contribute actively to school-wide, poly-wide, and industry engagement activities. Continuing Education & Training (CET) Develop and facilitate Continuing Education and Training (CET) programmes and professional workshops for adult learners and industry practitioners. What we are looking for Qualifications in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Analytics, Data Science, Business, Digital Innovation, or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant industry experience in one or more areas such as AI-enabled business transformation, digital innovation, business analytics, intelligent automation, product or service innovation, technology consulting, or AI solution implementation. Practical familiarity with generative AI, AI-assisted research and analysis, agentic AI, workflow automation, business intelligence, data visualisation, and/or AI-enabled solution prototyping. Sound understanding of responsible AI principles, AI ethics, governance, risk management, data privacy, cybersecurity, algorithmic bias, transparency, accountability, and human oversight. Strong communication, facilitation, analytical, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively in a dynamic environment. Passion for teaching, mentoring, and developing both pre-employment students and adult learners. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Adjunct Lecturer (Veterinary Technology / Veterinary Wellness Care) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Sustainability Finance) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 9999 Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineer Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Sep 2026 Lecturer (Architectural Technology & Building Services) / School of En Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Electronics) / School of Engi