      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 30 Sep 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics) / School of Informatics & IT What you will be working on Conduct full-time and part-time teaching in Information Technology, Networking, Cybersecurity, and other foundational ICT-related modules. Design, develop, review, and maintain curriculum, course materials, and assessments, while recommending enhancements to improve student learning outcomes, performance, and employability. Facilitate and guide student project work, including e-learning and self-directed learning initiatives, to develop technical and professional competencies. Provide coaching, mentoring, and academic guidance to support students’ learning, development, and success. Engage and collaborate with industry partners, parents, secondary schools, and other stakeholders to support outreach, partnership, and student development activities. What we are looking for Candidates with fewer years of relevant experience who demonstrate a strong aptitude and willingness to transition from other ICT-related disciplines will also be considered. Strong passion for education and a commitment to nurturing and imparting knowledge to youths and adult learners. Keen interest and willingness to acquire new knowledge and skills in cybersecurity and emerging ICT domains. Relevant professional IT or cybersecurity certifications will be an advantage but are not mandatory. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team, with an interest in mentoring and engaging youths and young adults. Possess strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Adjunct Lecturer (Veterinary Technology / Veterinary Wellness Care) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 Lecturer (Fashion Management & Design) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 12 Oct 2026 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (AI, Innovation) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Sep 2026 Lecturer (Electronics) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Nov 2026 Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineer Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Sep 2026 Lecturer (Information Technology) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Sep 2026 Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Veterinary Technology) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 15 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Cybersecurity & Digital Forensics) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Sep 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=temasek#/JobDescription/17842865/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-a0aa-90e604acf402": {
      "title": "Find A Job",
      "description": "Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Engineer (Enabling Technology Collaboratory) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Engineer (Enabling Technology Collaboratory) / School of Engineering What you will be working on Develop full-stack applications and integrate them with databases, cloud platforms, APIs and AI services. Design and deploy AI-enabled and agentic AI solutions leveraging AI/ML, LLMs, RAG, tool use and autonomous workflows. Integrate applications with devices, sensors, simulation systems and other digital platforms as required. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to gather requirements and propose suitable technical solutions. Contribute to applied research, consultancy projects and proposal development. Conduct PET and CET lessons, specialised courses, workshops and demonstrations. Supervise student projects and internships. Support project delivery, outreach activities and engagement with industry partners. What we are looking for Qualification in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electronics, Electrical Engineering, or a related discipline. At least 3 years of relevant industry or software development experience. Strong programming skills in one or more languages such as C#, Python, JavaScript/TypeScript, or C++. Hands-on experience in: o Full-stack web application development; o AI, ML, Gen AI and Agentic AI application development; o Cloud application deployment and integration. Ability to design maintainable software solutions and develop well-documented, reusable code. Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication and teamwork skills. Experience in client engagement, training delivery, student supervision, or technical proposal preparation will be advantageous. Familiarity with LLM APIs, RAG, tool integration, agent orchestration frameworks, or embodied AI will be an added advantage. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Senior/Scientist (Clean Energy Research Centre) / School of Engineerin Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Senior/Exec Engineer (Cement Treated-Mixed Materials Project Office) - National Environment Agency Closing in 5  day(s) Intern, Spring Buds Programme - Occupational Safety and Health Divisio MOM Closing on 10 Oct 2026 [LTA-RAOM] MANAGER, ASSET ENGINEERING (POWER & SERVICES) Land Transport Authority Closing on 08 Oct 2026 [PUB-WRP] AD/SE/EE Civil & Sitewide, PDCS Pub, Singapore's National Water Agency Closing in 3  day(s) [PUB-WRP] AD/SE/EE, Process, PDCS Pub, Singapore's National Water Agency Closing in 3  day(s) [PUB-WRP] Engineer/Executive/Senior Engineer (Process & Water Quality) Pub, Singapore's National Water Agency Closing in 4  day(s) [LTA-RSE] EXECUTIVE / ENGINEER, ELECTRICAL SERVICES (RAIL) Land Transport Authority Closing on 07 Oct 2026 Engineer (Enabling Technology Collaboratory) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic APPLY NOW"
